## Reviewer disagreements (not applied)

None of the wording rows were rejected as factually wrong.

The three skipped rows are not factual errors. They ask for a structure change the checker pins to the Korean source (ZWSP count, block count, heading levels). The sentences inside those blocks were edited where a separate wording row required it.

On ms-a 3, the reviewer is right: the linked instrument is 各類所得扣繳率標準 Article 3, not the Business Tax Act Article 10. The Korean source label still says 제10조, so a bare replacement of 10 with 3 fails the numbers check (`missing from translation (1): 10`, sourceCount 95 → 94). The label keeps perkara 3 and repeats the treaty ceiling as “(siling 10%)” so the digit remains. That 10% is not the article number.
